# Server-side and author-time files. `assets.directory` in wrangler.jsonc is
# the whole repository, so anything not listed here is uploaded as a public
# static file and can be fetched by URL. None of these are ever requested by
# a browser -- the Worker is bundled from `main` at deploy time rather than
# fetched from assets -- so excluding them changes nothing about how the site
# runs, and keeps the Worker's source (including the staff auth and the
# editor's admin API) from being downloadable.
#
# assets/ deliberately stays public: assets/js/content-address.js really is
# loaded by the browser, as part of the visual editor.
src
scripts
test
schema.sql
.dev.vars
EDITING-GUIDE.md
